# Production build settings.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle as a literal string, so
# a key set at build time is readable by anyone who opens the site or unzips the APK.
# It is not a secret once it is built. That fact decides everything below.
#
# This file used to force VITE_LLM_API_KEY empty, which made every production build
# keyless — including the APK, so the key had to be typed into Settings on the phone by
# hand, every install. That is a bad trade for a device you own.
#
# The arrangement now:
#
#   Local builds  read .env, which is gitignored and holds your key. `npm run apk` and
#                 a local `npm run build` therefore carry it, and the phone works the
#                 moment it is installed. build-apk.mjs prints a warning saying so.
#
#   CI builds     check out this repository, and .env is not in it. GitHub Pages is
#                 built with no key at all and stays safe to serve publicly. Visitors
#                 who want the language model paste their own key into Settings, where
#                 it lives in their own browser's localStorage.
#
# The consequence to remember: an APK built on a machine that has .env contains your
# key. Install it, do not publish it. To build a keyless one for sharing, run
# `npm run apk` with VITE_LLM_API_KEY= set in the environment, or move .env aside.
#
# Everything works with no key regardless — the tutor answers from its offline base and
# only reaches for a model when that base has nothing.

VITE_LLM_BUILD=production
